    "comparison": "Summary and Claim preserve the same operator-approved definition. Details in both preserve the same ID examples, prefix-scoped uniqueness/collision rule, lifecycle/version non-equivalence limit, and no dictionary/extractor/service requirement. M450 additionally clarifies literal names atom.id/projection.id, keeps them as distinct qualified names, and carries current Term//ID placement/authority constraints.",
    "uncovered_constraint_found": false,
    "authority_basis": "CA-R-1319 requires exactly one active Method Term Definition per Term; CA-E-659 checks Method Term Definition ownership and rejects Requirement-form definition; current M450 is the matching active Method owner.",
    "registry_decision": "Retain Term//ID and the global Term registry. The authorized manual source-retirement route may remove the exact Current CA-R-2275@2 carrier after M450 is the sole Current meaning owner; preserve the exact v2 preimage. Do not allocate a new R2275 version or claim a native archive workflow."
  },
